AWS-008 — Workflow Lifecycle

Document ID: AWS-008
Title: Workflow Lifecycle
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Workflow Lifecycle Model (CWLM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Workflow Lifecycle Model establishes the governed progression of Workflow Definitions, Workflow Instances, and Workflow Programs throughout their operational existence while preserving traceability, governance, reproducibility, and engineering intent.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Workflow Definition lifecycle
Workflow Instance lifecycle
Workflow Program lifecycle
Lifecycle transitions
Activation
Suspension
Retirement
Lifecycle governance

This specification applies to every Canonical Workflow Object.

3. Canonical Definition

A Workflow Lifecycle is the governed sequence of operational states through which a workflow artifact progresses from creation through retirement while preserving identity, governance, traceability, and historical continuity.

The lifecycle governs workflow evolution.

It does not govern workflow execution semantics.

4. Objectives

The Workflow Lifecycle Model SHALL:

Standardize workflow evolution.
Preserve engineering intent.
Enable controlled publication.
Support safe activation.
Enable retirement.
Preserve historical continuity.
Support governance.
Enable reproducibility.
5. Lifecycle Principles

Every workflow lifecycle SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Explicit Progression

Lifecycle transitions SHALL be explicitly governed.

Immutable Releases

Published Workflow Definitions SHALL remain immutable.

Traceable Evolution

Every lifecycle transition SHALL preserve workflow lineage.

Separation of Definition and Execution

Workflow Definition lifecycles SHALL remain independent of Workflow Instance lifecycles.

Historical Preservation

Retired workflow artifacts SHALL remain permanently reconstructable.

Governed Change

Lifecycle transitions SHALL follow applicable Canonical Policy Objects.

6. Workflow Definition Lifecycle

Atlas defines the following canonical lifecycle for Workflow Definitions.

State	Description
Draft	Under authoring
Review	Technical review
Approved	Governance approval completed
Published	Available for execution
Active	Authorized for instantiation
Deprecated	Scheduled for replacement
Retired	No longer available for new execution
Archived	Historical preservation

Workflow Definitions SHALL remain versioned.

7. Workflow Instance Lifecycle

Workflow Instances follow a different lifecycle.

State	Description
Created	Instance created
Initialized	Context resolved
Running	Execution active
Waiting	Awaiting trigger or dependency
Suspended	Execution paused
Recovering	Failure recovery
Completed	Successfully finished
Failed	Unrecoverable failure
Cancelled	Intentionally terminated
Archived	Historical record

Instances SHALL preserve complete execution history.

8. Workflow Program Lifecycle

Workflow Programs coordinate multiple Workflow Instances.

Atlas defines the following lifecycle.

State	Description
Planned	Program defined
Approved	Governance approval
Activated	Program initiated
Executing	Coordinated execution
Monitoring	Progress oversight
Completed	Program objectives achieved
Closed	Administrative completion
Archived	Historical preservation

Programs SHALL remain independently governed.

