Lifecycle transitions SHALL remain permanently auditable.

10. Activation

Workflow activation SHALL require:

Approved Workflow Definition
Compatible Policy Baseline
Valid Execution Context
Required participants
Required resources
Applicable governance approval

Activation SHALL create a Workflow Instance.

11. Suspension and Recovery

Workflow suspension MAY occur due to:

Manual intervention
Policy decision
Resource unavailability
External dependency
Security event
Operational maintenance

Recovery SHALL preserve execution consistency and historical traceability.

12. Retirement

Workflow retirement SHALL define:

Retirement authority
Retirement rationale
Effective date
Successor workflow (if applicable)
Migration guidance
Retention period

Retirement SHALL NOT invalidate historical Workflow Instances.

13. Lifecycle Events

Lifecycle activities MAY generate Canonical Events.

Examples include:

Workflow Draft Created
Workflow Approved
Workflow Published
Workflow Activated
Workflow Suspended
Workflow Completed
Workflow Retired

Events SHALL conform to ADS-006 — Canonical Event (CEV).

14. Lifecycle Governance

Every workflow lifecycle SHALL define:

Workflow owner
Steward
Review authority
Approval authority
Retirement authority
Governance domain
Applicable policies

Lifecycle governance SHALL remain independently auditable.

15. Lifecycle Quality

Every workflow lifecycle SHALL satisfy:

Correctness
Traceability
Reproducibility
Governance compliance
Auditability
Explainability
Consistency
Completeness

Quality SHALL be continuously evaluated.

16. Conformance

A Workflow Lifecycle implementation conforms if it:

Implements canonical lifecycle states.
Preserves immutable workflow definitions.
Separates definition and instance lifecycles.
Supports governed activation.
Maintains complete lifecycle history.
Preserves workflow lineage.
Supports retirement and archival.
17. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-assisted lifecycle management.
Predictive workflow retirement.
Autonomous lifecycle governance.
Cross-federation lifecycle synchronization.
Dynamic activation policies.
Continuous workflow evolution.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical lifecycle semantics.

